\value{
\code{as_diffusion()} returns a 'diffusionModel' object
(with the class 'diff_model' second, for compatibility),
a table of the number of nodes in each value of the attribute at each step,
from the start of the diffusion.
The table has a column for each value, and a column of the new nodes in
each value (for example \code{I} and \code{I_new}).
A record in S, E, I, and R always has these four columns,
and \code{s} counts the susceptible nodes that are exposed.
The table keeps the name of the attribute in \code{attr(, "attribute")},
and the roles of its values in \code{attr(, "compartments")},
where these are known.
By default, a compact version of the component table is printed
(to print all the changes at each time point, use \code{print(..., verbose = T)}).
To retrieve the diffusion events table, use \code{summary(...)}.
